<section class="saas-legal-page">
  <div class="saas-container saas-page-shell">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="saas-breadcrumbs">
      <.link navigate={~p"/"}>Home</.link>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Photo to Sticker</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="saas-page-hero">
      <p class="saas-legal-kicker">Photo to Sticker</p>
      <h1>Turn Any Photo into a Sticker</h1>
      <p class="saas-value-strip">
        Free &middot; 3 generations without an account &middot; PNG &amp; WebP download
      </p>
      <p>
        Photo to sticker conversion turns an ordinary picture into a sticker-style image you can
        use in chats, on profiles, or in thumbnails. Upload a photo below and generate your first
        sticker without creating an account.
      </p>
      <a class="saas-button saas-button-primary" href="/?mode=portrait#generator">Upload a Photo</a>
      <p class="saas-tool-note">No account needed &middot; 3 free guest generations</p>
    </div>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to turn a photo into a sticker</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Upload a JPG or PNG photo up to 8 MB. No account is required for 3 free guest generations.</li>
        <li>Add an optional prompt to steer the style, or leave it blank for the default sticker look.</li>
        <li>Generate. Each photo generation uses 1 credit and failed generations return the credit.</li>
        <li>Download the sticker as PNG or WebP, then resize it for the app where you plan to use it.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>What photos work best</h2>
      <p>
        The generator reads the photo you provide, so a clear source gives you more control over the
        result. A bright, front-facing image with the subject filling most of the frame usually
        produces the most predictable sticker artwork.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Use</strong> sharp, well-lit photos where the subject is easy to identify.</li>
        <li><strong>Use</strong> the largest clear version available; compressed screenshots lose detail.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid</strong> heavy motion blur, very dark lighting, and subjects cropped at the edge.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid</strong> busy backgrounds when you want a clean cutout-style silhouette.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Photo to sticker styles and examples</h2>
      <p>
        The same source photo can produce different results depending on the subject and prompt.
        Use the following directions to choose a useful starting point.
      </p>
      <h3>Portrait photos</h3>
      <p>Faces convert well when they are front-facing and evenly lit. Ask for a clean outline, simple background, or profile avatar when you want the face to remain readable at a small size.</p>
      <h3>Pet photos</h3>
      <p>Pets are forgiving subjects because fur and rounded shapes suit sticker artwork. An eye-level photo with the animal facing the camera gives a clean result.</p>
      <h3>Couple and group photos</h3>
      <p>Two subjects can work when they are close together and similarly lit. Larger groups become harder to read at sticker size, so crop to the main subjects when possible.</p>
      <h3>Product photos</h3>
      <p>Product shots can become clean silhouettes with a subtle shadow. Use a plain background and even lighting, then inspect reflective or transparent products carefully.</p>
      <h3>Logo and mascot photos</h3>
      <p>Photographed logos and mascots can be restyled into stickers, although flat graphics with hard edges are more predictable than reflective surfaces.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Photo to sticker for WhatsApp, Telegram and Discord</h2>
      <p>
        AI Sticker Maker generates the artwork and gives you a downloadable file. Outputs are
        typically 1024 x 1024 px, while chat platforms apply their own dimensions, formats,
        transparency, and file-size rules. Resizing is part of the platform workflow.
      </p>
      <p>Telegram's sticker creation guide accepts PNG or WebP with one side at exactly 512 pixels and the other at 512 pixels or less. Telegram recommends transparency, while some import workflows add transparency and file-size requirements, so check the upload method you use.</p>
      <p>WhatsApp sticker workflows commonly require 512 x 512 px WebP files, transparency, and strict file-size limits. Discord custom stickers also apply their own dimensions, format, size, and server requirements. Confirm the current rules before finalizing a pack.</p>
      <p>A practical workflow is to generate here, download PNG, resize it for the destination, and convert or remove the background in an image editor when a platform requires it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Turn a photo into a sticker on iPhone or Android</h2>
      <p>Choose the clearest original photo available on your phone. A camera image usually contains more useful detail than a screenshot or compressed social download. Keep the prompt short so it is easy to revise on a small screen.</p>
      <p>Built-in phone cutout features are useful when you only need a simple extraction. Use a photo sticker generator when you want the source restyled, several stylistic variations, or a PNG or WebP file that can be edited and uploaded elsewhere.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Output formats: PNG and WebP</h2>
      <p>Every finished sticker can be downloaded as PNG or WebP. PNG is the safer default for editing and broad compatibility. WebP produces smaller files for websites, galleries, previews, and chat workflows.</p>
      <p>If your project requires a strictly transparent background, open the downloaded file in an image editor and confirm the alpha channel before production use. See <.link navigate={~p"/transparent-sticker-maker"}>PNG and WebP download options</.link> for more format guidance.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Photo sticker prompt examples</h2>
      <p>Prompts are optional, but naming the palette, outline, and background gives more consistent results across a set of stickers.</p>
      <div class="saas-prompt-list">
        <code>family photo sticker, warm colors, soft outline, simple background</code>
        <code>pet portrait sticker, fluffy texture, rounded frame, bright palette</code>
        <code>product photo sticker, clean silhouette, subtle shadow, white border</code>
        <code>couple photo sticker, matching style, playful expressions, bold edge</code>
        <code>logo photo sticker, flat colors, sharp edges, centered composition</code>
        <code>travel photo sticker, cheerful mood, crisp outline, minimal detail</code>
        <code>baby photo sticker, pastel palette, soft rounded edges, plain background</code>
        <code>friend group sticker, cartoon style, consistent line weight, light background</code>
        <code>food photo sticker, glossy highlights, thick outline, transparent-friendly</code>
        <code>seasonal photo sticker, festive palette, decorative border, simple shapes</code>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Photo to sticker FAQ</h2>
      <div class="saas-faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>How do I turn a photo into a sticker?</summary>
          <p>Upload a JPG or PNG photo, add an optional prompt, and generate. The finished sticker appears in your history as a PNG or WebP file.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What photo formats and sizes can I upload?</summary>
          <p>Upload JPG or PNG images up to 8 MB. Use the largest clear version available; compressed screenshots give the generator less detail.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How many photos can I convert for free?</summary>
          <p>Guests get 3 free generations with no sign up. Each photo generation uses 1 credit.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need an account to turn a photo into a sticker?</summary>
          <p>No. Guest results remain available through the current guest identity. Sign in to buy credits and attach eligible results to your account.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What happens if a generation fails?</summary>
          <p>The credit is returned automatically. Upload-based stickers save a private source image so a failed generation can be retried without uploading again.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use photo stickers commercially?</summary>
          <p>Review the <.link navigate={~p"/terms-of-service"}>terms of service</.link> for the current usage terms before using generated stickers in paid or branded work.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I turn a photo into a WhatsApp sticker directly?</summary>
          <p>Not in one step. Generate and download here first, then resize and convert the file to the destination platform's current requirements.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Related tools</h2>
      <div class="saas-related-links">
        <.link navigate={~p"/face-to-sticker"}>Face to Sticker</.link>
